<article class="env-lemma" id="0CZR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CZR">Lemma <span data-tag="0CZR">37.16.8</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite presentation. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a finitely presented $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module flat over $S$. Then the set </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \{ x \in X : \mathcal{F}\text{ free in a neighbourhood of }x\}   \]
</div>
  <p> is open in $X$ and its formation commutes with arbitrary base change $S' \to S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Openness holds trivially. Let $x \in X$ mapping to $s \in S$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/080Q" data-tag="080Q">37.16.7</a> we see that $x$ is in our set if and only if $\mathcal{F}|_{X_ s}$ is flat at $x$ over $X_ s$. Clearly this is also equivalent to $\mathcal{F}$ being flat at $x$ over $X$ (because this statement is implied by freeness of $\mathcal{F}_ x$ and implies flatness of $\mathcal{F}|_{X_ s}$ at $x$ over $X_ s$). Thus the base change statement follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/05VJ" data-tag="05VJ">37.16.5</a> applied to $\text{id} : X \to X$ over $S$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>